  "findings": [
    "obligation_coverage: The target needs seven principal interfaces, not just volume. The existing [seven-route map](knowledge/overview.md#reader-entrance-and-available-operations) includes local directional, trace, ball, index, covering and triangle operations. The new plans will assign full radial derivations and bounded global mechanisms without promoting imports.",
    "fast_route_reconstruction: Relative current expansion controls logarithmic density; division by the positive model density yields ray order, then cutting and weighted averaging yield ball order. This recovers the [six transitions](knowledge/overview.md#ricci-lower-bounds-to-ball-volume) without invoking matrix order.",
    "slow_step_reproduction: From N prime=q w and W prime=w, direct division gives F prime=(w/W)(q-F); q(t)>=q(r) proves F(r)>=q(r). Local absolute continuity allows integration. The [weighted-average subsection](knowledge/nodes/N-M-cut-integration.md#a-positive-weighted-average) contains exactly these hypotheses and operations.",
    "condition_transfer: Removing cut truncation loses multiplicity one, reversing Ricci leaves the negative traceless-square term uncontrolled, and dropping simple connectivity preserves a covering but loses injectivity. The [trace boundary](knowledge/nodes/N-M-trace.md#what-the-hypotheses-do-not-give) distinguishes proof failure from the separately calculated cylinder/product counterexamples."
  ],
